  "question": {
    "text": "The resistance of the series combination of two resistors is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math>. When they are joined in parallel the equivalent resistance becomes&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>nP</mi></math>, then the minimum possible value of <em><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math></em> is"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "In series combination,&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br />In parallel combination,&nbsp; <math> <mrow> <mtext>P</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>R</mtext> <mn>1</mn> </msub> <msub> <mtext>R</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>R</mtext> <mn>1</mn> </msub> <mo>+</mo> <msub> <mtext>R</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>nP</mi></math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#8756;</mo> </mrow> </math> &nbsp; <math> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>R</mtext> <mn>1</mn> </msub> <mo>+</mo> <msub> <mtext>R</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </mfenced>&#160; &#160; <mo>=</mo> <mtext>n</mtext> <mfrac> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>R</mtext> <mn>1</mn> </msub> <msub> <mtext>R</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>R</mtext> <mn>1</mn> </msub> <mo>+</mo> <msub> <mtext>R</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#8756;</mo> </mrow> </math> &nbsp;&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>R</mtext> <mn>1</mn> </msub> <mo>+</mo> <msub> <mtext>R</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>=</mo> <mtext>n</mtext> <msub> <mtext>R</mtext> <mn>1</mn> </msub> <msub> <mtext>R</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math><br /><br />For minimum value, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mtext>R</mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext>R</mtext></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mtext>n</mtext><mfenced><mrow><mtext>R</mtext><mo>&#215;</mo><mtext>R</mtext></mrow></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mtext>R</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mtext>nR</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mtext>&#8658;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>"
  }
